Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||06-07-2001||12:40 PM||||Another little head ache... finally got the car into the shop yestarday, unfortunatly there were no lifts open so I had to do everything on the ground w/ jack stands, but anyways. For some time now (last 2 weeks or so) sometimes while steering/breaking at low speeds (parking lot maneuvers) I can here and barily feel a 'thunk' coming from the front end. sometimes it seams to be one wheel or another, sometimes it feels like both. I've got new lower ball joints, all poly bushings, new shocks, and a fresh alignment. while I was in the shop, I lifted each side up to try and find any loose parts, (or a bent a frame) but every thing looks fine, the only movement was in the rubber boot area of the stearing rack, it would shift about 1/8-1/4 inch up and down when I hit the tired, but no obvious sounds. any clues? upper ball joint looked good, the boots on the tie rod ends are cracked, but they're still holding stiff. Anyways, it's an 88 formula, just trying to figure this out befor I have to drive it to Wisconsin. Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||06-07-2001||01:00 PM||||I'm guessing rack bushings are worn, or the shaft that holds your upper control arms is moving around. If the bolts get loose, it can slide the length of the slots. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000002||ThatRickGuy||06-08-2001||08:43 AM||||Hey found the problem! There is a 1/8 gap between the poly from the new lower bushings and the housing, looks like the brain child at the auto shop put the bushings in backwards or something. so, now I get to go argue w/ them over it this afternoon. ||||reg||1
