Z||000012||ThatRickGuy||06-12-2001||11:50 AM||||Okay, another update. Talked to the Fierostore's helpdesk today, they're awesome! anyways. We compared numbers and they looked the same. But he knew what was wrong, sounded like he had heard of mechanics doing this before. Who ever the mechanic who replaced my bushings was, pulled the metal sleaves out w/ the old bushings, and didn't put it back in w/ the new bushings, so there is no housing arround the bushing. I've been trying to get a hold of the Owner of the shop all morning, the manager is incompetent and never calls back. First the manager said he was 'busy' and he'd have him call me in a few minutes. 45 minutes later I called back and the manager clamed the owner was on an 'Extended Test Drive'. It bothers me that he didn't call me knowing that he was going to be out of the shop, and also, what the H-E-doubble hockey sticks is an 'extended test drive'? I thought I was just imagining the fact that my gas guage seemed a little lower when I got my car back, now I'm wondering if someone didn't take a little ride in my car.||||reg||1
Z||000013||DecadenceR||06-12-2001||12:54 PM||||I used to work at a pretty shady shop like that. Well, that's what it sounds like from your instance anyway. They used to take extended test drives...<BR>One guy took a customer's car over the weekend.<BR>Anyway, I'd get ahold of the local branch of the BBB if I were you, and lodge a complaint. It's not the best way to get back at them, but it's a start.||||reg||1
